hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17103","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Awzai, he said: Rabiah ibn Yazid narrated to me, he said: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us and said: Do you claim that I am the last of you to die? Nay, I am the first of you to die, and you will follow me in scattered bands, some of you destroying others."
"17104","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to me, he said: Wathilah ibn al-Asqa invited me, and his sight had gone, and he said: O Khabbab, lead me to Yazid ibn al-Aswad al-Jurashi. Then he mentioned the hadith. He said: Give glad tidings, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say from Allah, Mighty and Majestic: I am as My servant thinks Me to be, so let him think of Me as he wills."
"17105","Issam ibn Khalid and Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, they said: Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd Allah al-Nasri, he said: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa say: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the greatest fabrications is that a man be claimed to other than his father, or that he show his two eyes in a dream what they did not see, or that he say upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, what he did not say."
"17106","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Khawlani narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Rubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri say: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa mention that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman takes three inheritances: her freed slave, her foundling, and the child over whom she invoked lian."
"17107","Sulayman ibn Dawud Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was given in place of the Torah the Seven, and I was given in place of the Psalms the Miin, and I was given in place of the Gospel the Mathani, and I was favored with the Mufassal."
"17108","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Said, meaning Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah say: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The greatest fabrication is one who attributes to me what I did not say, and one who shows his two eyes in a dream what they did not see, and one who claims himself to other than his father."
"17109","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Imran Abu al-Awwam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The scriptures of Ibrahim, peace be upon him, were sent down on the first night of Ramadan, and the Torah was sent down after six nights had passed of Ramadan, and the Gospel after thirteen nights had elapsed of Ramadan, and the Furqan was sent down after twenty-four nights had elapsed of Ramadan."
"17110","Arim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from al-Gharif ibn Ayyash, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, he said: A group of Banu Sulaym came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: A companion of ours has made it obligatory. He said: Let him free a slave; Allah will ransom with every limb of it a limb of him from the Fire."
"17111","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: Abu Ammar Shaddad narrated to me, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah chose Kinanah from the sons of Ismail, and chose Quraysh from the sons of Kinanah, and chose Banu Hashim from Quraysh, and chose me from Banu Hashim."
"17112","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from Shaddad Abu Ammar, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, chose from the children of Ibrahim, Ismail, and chose from the sons of Ismail, Kinanah, and chose from the sons of Kinanah, Quraysh, and chose from Quraysh, Banu Hashim, and chose me from Banu Hashim."
"17113","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from Shaddad Abu Ammar, he said: I entered upon Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, and with him was a people, and they mentioned Ali. When they stood up, he said to me: Shall I not inform you of what I saw from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? I said: Yes. He said: I came to Fatimah, may Allah Most High be pleased with her, asking her about Ali. She said: He went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I sat waiting for him until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, and with him were Ali and Hasan and Husayn, may Allah Most High be pleased with them, holding each one of the two by his hand until he entered. Then he brought Ali and Fatimah near and seated them before him, and seated Hasan and Husayn, each one of the two upon his thigh. Then he wrapped over them his garment, or he said: a cloak. Then he recited this verse: Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly. And he said: O Allah, these are the people of my house, and the people of my house are most entitled."
"17114","Ziyad ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Kathir al-Shami, of the people of Palestine, narrated to us, from a woman of them called Fasilah, that she said: I heard my father say: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it part of tribalism that a man love his people? He said: No, but part of tribalism is that a man aid his people upon injustice. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I heard one of the people of knowledge mention that her father, meaning Fasilah, is Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, and I saw my father place this hadith at the end of the hadiths of Wathilah, so I thought he appended it to the hadith of Wathilah."
